# prose-audit: Grade A — The documentary, Sejm resolution, Church hierarchy and survivors now create a concrete conflict, with distinct costs and aftermaths for every Lewica response.
title: A saint in the chamber
face-image: img/poland/events/john-paul-ii-monument.webp
new-page: true
on-arrival: church_2023_done = 1; cultural_issue_salience += 7; news_headline = "A dispute over John Paul II becomes a loyalty test"

= March 2023 — What the nation is allowed to remember

**Marcin Gutowski**, a TVN24 investigative journalist, asks what Karol Wojtyła
knew about abusive priests before he became Pope John Paul II. His report draws
partly on communist-era files, which makes scrutiny necessary and certainty
hard.

PiS answers with a Sejm resolution defending the pope's name. Bishops speak of
an attack on Poland; survivors hear the state protecting an institution before
it has listened to them. For Lewica, the question is no longer whether Church
power should be examined, but how to do it without turning history into another
tribal oath.

